    "photo_reviews_1": {
      "type": "dewy-photo-reviews",
      "blocks": {
        "photo_1": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260813_132010_5f6ef4d3-c3e4-4a9c-8bbf-6a61ddaf4b0c.png",
            "name": "Joshua K.",
            "rating": 5,
            "quote": "I noticed my first grey hairs in my early 30s and honestly thought I was imagining them. Then there were more. By the time I started getting them around my temples, I was constantly checking my hair in the mirror before going anywhere. I hated the whole process of buying dye, mixing it, making a mess, and finding time to actually do it. I tried this shampoo almost as a last resort because I liked the idea of just using it in the shower. After the first few uses, the grey hairs looked much less noticeable and my hair looked darker and shinier overall. What I like most is that I don't have to make 'dyeing my hair' an entire event anymore."
          }
        },
        "photo_2": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260813_132033_643a3022-7e2c-4639-b742-a6145f5541c5.png",
            "name": "Jessica P.",
            "rating": 4.5,
            "quote": "For years I had a little routine every few weeks — book the appointment, sit at the salon, pay for the colour, then start worrying about the roots again a few weeks later. It wasn't even the money that bothered me most. I was tired of constantly thinking about my grey roots. A friend told me about black dye shampoo and I figured I had nothing to lose. I started using it in the shower and gradually noticed the white strands blending into the rest of my hair. It's definitely changed my routine. Now instead of feeling like I'm constantly chasing my roots, I have something quick I can use when they start becoming noticeable."
          }
        },
        "photo_3": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260813_132056_5dd3e734-bf4f-4697-9a67-5fdad992515d.png",
            "name": "Anthony A.",
            "rating": 5,
            "quote": "My hair started going grey much earlier than I expected, and I didn't realize how much it was affecting my confidence until I started avoiding photos. I'd position myself so the grey around my hairline wasn't showing and would check the mirror before leaving the house. Traditional hair dye always felt like too much work, so I decided to try a wash-in colour shampoo. I wasn't expecting perfection after one wash, but after using it a few times my hair looked noticeably darker and the grey was much less obvious. The biggest difference wasn't really my hair — it was that I stopped thinking about it every time someone took a picture. That alone made me glad I tried it."
          }
        },
        "photo_4": {
          "type": "photo_review",
          "settings": {
            "photo": "shopify://shop_images/hf_20260813_132105_64e35868-fa20-4722-8053-b3ba738ff139.png",
            "name": "Amy L.",
            "rating": 5,
            "quote": "I started noticing more grey whenever I washed my hair, and eventually I got tired of pretending I didn't care. I wasn't ready to spend hours at a salon every few weeks, but I also didn't want my hair looking patchy. I saw this dye shampoo and figured I'd give it a try because using it in the shower sounded so much easier. The first time I wasn't expecting much, but after using it a few times, the grey around my temples became much harder to notice. Now I keep it in the shower and use it as part of my normal routine. It's funny — I used to plan my hair appointments around when my roots would show. Now I barely think about them."
          }
        }
      },
